The boundary consists of three semicircular arcs meeting at the vertices of the triangle.
The candidates for the maximum distance are between:
1. Two vertices of the triangle (distance 2).
2. Two points diametrically opposite on the semicircles (distance 2 within one semicircle, but points are on boundary).
3. A "tip" of one semicircle (midpoint of arc) and a vertex of the triangle not on that semicircle.
4. Two tips of different semicircles.
