{"code": "from itertools import combinations\n\n# Define the components based on the trace\nnodes_c2 = {3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9, 10, 12, 15, 16, 18, 20, 24, 30, 36, 40, 45, 48}\nedges_c2 = [\n    (3, 6), (4, 12), (5, 20), (6, 12), (6, 30), \n    (8, 24), (9, 18), (10, 15), (10, 40), \n    (12, 24), (12, 36), (15, 30), (16, 48), \n    (18, 36), (20, 30), (24, 40), (24, 48), \n    (30, 45), (36, 45)\n]\n\nnodes_c3 = {7, 21, 28, 42}\nedges_c3 = [(7, 42), (21, 28), (21, 42)]\n\nnodes_c6 = {14, 35}\nedges_c6 = [(14, 35)]\n\n# Function to compute Max Independent Set\n# Since N is small per component, we can use brute force with bitmask\n\ndef compute_mis(graph_nodes, graph_edges):\n    nodes_list = sorted(list(graph_nodes))\n    n = len(nodes_list)\n    node_to_idx = {node: i for i, node in enumerate(nodes_list)}\n    \n    # Build adjacency bitmask\n    adj = [0] * n\n    for u, v in graph_edges:\n        if u in node_to_idx and v in node_to_idx:\n            i, j = node_to_idx[u], node_to_idx[v]\n            adj[i] |= (1 << j)\n            adj[j] |= (1 << i)\n            \n    max_is = 0\n    \n    # Iterate through all subsets\n    # Optimization: iterate only through independent sets? \n    # Or just iterate 2^n. 2^18 = 262k, feasible.\n    for mask in range(1 << n):\n        # Check if independent\n        is_valid = True\n        for i in range(n):\n            if (mask >> i) & 1:\n                if adj[i] & mask:\n                    is_valid = False\n                    break\n        if is_valid:\n            count = bin(mask).count('1')\n            if count > max_is:\n                max_is = count\n    return max_is\n\nmis_c2 = compute_mis(nodes_c2, edges_c2)\nmis_c3 = compute_mis(nodes_c3, edges_c3)\nmis_c6 = compute_mis(nodes_c6, edges_c6)\n\nprint(f\"MIS(C2) = {mis_c2}\")\nprint(f\"MIS(C3) = {mis_c3}\")\nprint(f\"MIS(C6) = {mis_c6}\")\n\n# Number of isolated vertices (components of size 1)\n# Total vertices = 50\n# Vertices in components = 18 + 4 + 2 = 24\n# Isolated = 50 - 24 = 26\nisolated_count = 50 - (len(nodes_c2) + len(nodes_c3) + len(nodes_c6))\n\nprint(f\"Isolated count = {isolated_count}\")\n\nmax_subset_size = mis_c2 + mis_c3 + mis_c6 + isolated_count\nprint(f\"Maximum subset size with no valid pairs (M) = {max_subset_size}\")\nprint(f\"Smallest K = M + 1 = {max_subset_size + 1}\")"}

