here are 6 runs. Since $k=6$, the number of H runs and T runs differ by at most 1.\nPossible configurations for $(k_H, k_T)$: $(3, 3)$ or $(4, 2)$ or $(2, 4)$. But since runs alternate, if start with H, then $k_H = k_T$ or $k_H = k_T + 1$. If start with T, $k_T = k_H$ or $k_T = k_H + 1$.\nSince sum is 8 and $k=6$, the only possibilities are $k_H=3, k_T=3$ (starts with H, ends with T or starts with T ends with H) OR $k_H=4, k_T=2$ (impossible, must alternate $H,T,H,T,H,T,H$ -> 4H 3T? No. H T H T H T has 3H 3T. H T H T H T H has 4H 3T). Wait, if $k=6$, possible splits are (3,3). \nIf $k_H=4, k_T=2$, then $k=6$. Sequence H T H T H T H -> 4 H runs, 3 T runs. Sum $k=7$. We need $k=6$. \nLet's re-evaluate. \nSum of lengths = $\\sum_{runs} (L_r - 1) + k = (1) + (1) + (k-2) = k + 2 = 8 \\implies k=6$. Correct.\nTotal runs = 6. \nAlternating types. So either $k_H=3, k_T=3$ (starts with H, ends with T; or starts T ends H) OR... wait. If it starts with H: H, T, H, T, H, T -> 3 H, 3 T. If H, T, H, T, H, T, H -> 4 H, 3 T (k=7). So for $k=6$, it must be 3 of one and 3 of the other. \nSo the sequence has 3 Head runs and 3 Tail runs. \nOne Head run has length 2, two have length 1. One Tail run has length 2, two have length 1.\nTotal permutations of run lengths?\nWe need to choose which H-run is length 2 (3 choices) and which T-run is length 2 (3 choices). \nAlso need to consider starting with H or T. \n\nScenario A: Starts with H. Sequence of run types: H, T, H, T, H, T. \nRuns: $r_1(H), r_2(T), r_3(H), r_4(T), r_5(H), r_6(T)$. \nLengths: One of $\r_1, \r_3, \r_5$ is 2, others 1. One of $\r_2, \r_4, \r_6$ is 2, others 1. \nNumber of ways to assign lengths: $3 \\times 3 = 9$.\nEach specific set of lengths corresponds to a unique sequence of flip outcomes (since run lengths determine the sequence uniquely). \nSo 9 sequences starting with H.\nScenario B: Starts with T. Sequence of run types: T, H, T, H, T, H. \nRuns: $r_1(T), r_2(H), r_3(T), r_4(H), r_5(T), r_6(H)$. \nOne of $\r_2, \r