[[ ## next_thought ## ]]
The Python script has defined the strategy to find the optimal set. It iterates over the size $m$ of the set, calculates the starting number $k$ for a consecutive sequence, and then distributes the remainder $r = 2021 - \text{sum}(k, \dots, k+m-1)$ by adding 1 to the largest $r$ elements to maintain the sum 2021 with distinct integers. This is the standard greedy approach for maximizing the product of distinct integers with a fixed sum. The script computes the product and the exponent of 2 in the prime factorization of the product.

