Wait, the noise calculation:
$Var(x) = 60^2/12 = 300$.
$y = x + noise$.
$Var(y) = 300 + V_n$.
$Cov(x,y) = Var(x) = 300$.
$\rho = 300 / \sqrt{300(300+V_n)} = 1/\sqrt{1+V_n/300}$.
$1+V_n/300 = 1/\rho^2 \implies V_n/300 = 1/\rho^2 - 1$.
For $\rho=0.6$, $V_n = 300(1/0.36 - 1) = 300(1.777) = 533$. Std = 23.08.
For $\rho=0.5$, $V_n = 300(3) = 900$. Std = 30.
My code used 23 and 67 (error).
Correct for 0.5: 30.
