  "reasoning": "Let the vertices of the cube be identified with the set $V = \\{0, 1\\}^3$. Two vertices are neighbors if they differ in exactly one coordinate. The condition is: for any vertex $v$, if all neighbors of $v$ have color $c$, then $v$ must also have color $c$. We consider the color of $v$ as $f(v) \\in \\{B, W\\}$. The condition is the negation of the existence of a monochromatic neighborhood leading to a different color at the center.\n\nLet's analyze the constraints. Suppose there is a vertex $v$ with color B. If all its neighbors are B, then $v$ must be B (which is consistent). If all its neighbors are W, then $v$ must be W (contradiction, since $v$ is B). So, if a vertex is B and has at least one B neighbor, it doesn't force anything. However, if a vertex is B and has a neighborhood consisting entirely of W's, that is forbidden. Similarly for W.\n\nLet's rephrase: The condition forbids a local pattern where a vertex has a monochromatic neighborhood of a different color. \nConsider the function $f: \\{0,1\\}^3 \\to \\{0, 1\\}$ (mapping colors to 0/1). The condition is: $\\forall v, (\\forall u \\sim v, f(u) = c) \\implies f(v) = c$.\n\nLet's test small sub-configurations or use symmetry.\nCase 1: All vertices same color. (2 ways). Valid? Yes. Neighbors of any are same, so self is same.\nCase 2: Two colors present.\nSuppose there is exactly one vertex of color A and seven of color B. Let the single A vertex be $v$. Its neighbors are 3. They are all B. So the condition at $v$ is: 'all neighbors are B' implies $v$ is B. But $v$ is A. So this is invalid.\nGenerally, if there is a vertex $v$ of color A such that all its neighbors are B, it is invalid. So, no vertex of any color can be surrounded by the opposite color.\nSimilarly, no vertex of color B can be surrounded by A.\n\nThis means that for every vertex $v$, the set of colors of its neighbors must not be a singleton different from $f(v)$. \nIf $f(v) = 0$, neighbors cannot be all 1. If $f(v) = 1$, neighbors cannot be all 0.\n\nLet $N(v)$ be the neighbor set of $v$. The condition is $f(v) = \\text{majority}(N(v))$? Not quite. If neighbors are mixed (0,1), then the condition \"all neighbors are same\" is false, so no constraint on $f(v)$. \nThe constraint only applies if $N(v)$ is monochromatic. \nSo, we cannot have $v$ surrounded by 0s while $v=1$. We cannot have $v$ surrounded by 1s while $v=0$.\n\nThis implies that if a vertex is isolated from its color (surrounded by opposite), it's bad. \nConsider the subgraph of vertices of color 0. Let this be $S_0$. If $v \\in S_0$, and $N(v) \\subseteq S_1$, then $v$ is invalid. So no vertex in $S_0$ can have all neighbors in $S_1$. Similarly for $S_1$.\nIn a cube, degree is 3. \nIf $S_0$ is the whole set, ok. \nIf $S_0$ is not empty and not all, say $|S_0|=k$. \nIf there exists $v \\in S_0$ whose neighbors are in $S_1$, invalid. So every vertex in $S_0$ must have at least one neighbor in $S_0$. This means $S_0$ has no isolated vertices in the induced subgraph on $S_0$. I.e., the minimum degree in the subgraph induced by $S_0$ is $\\ge 1$. \nAlso, the subgraph induced by $S_1$ must have minimum degree $\\ge 1$.\n\nLet's check possible sizes of $S_0$. $k = |S_0|$. $S_1$ has size $8-k$.\n$k=0$: $S_0=\\emptyset$. Valid (1 way, plus $S_0=V$). Total 2. \n$k=1$: Let $S_0 = \\{v\\}$. Neighbors of $v$ are 3, all in $S_1$. So $v$ is surrounded by opposite. Invalid. \n$k=2$: Let $S_0 = \\{u, v\\}$. \nSubcase 2a: $u, v$ are adjacent. Then $u$ has neighbor $v \\in S_0$, so not all neighbors in $S_1$. $v$ similarly. What about other vertices? No restriction on $S_1$ vertices from $S_0$. We need to check if any $w \\in S_1$ is surrounded by $S_0$. $w$ has 3 neighbors. $S_0$ has size 2. Impossible for $w$ to have 3 neighbors in $S_0$. So $S_1$ vertices are safe. Thus, any pair of adjacent vertices as $S_0$ is valid. Number of edges in cube = 12. So 12 colorings. \nSubcase 2b: $u, v$ are not adjacent (distance 2). They share a common neighbor $w$. $u$'s neighbors: $v$ (no), $w$, and one other $x$. If $S_0 = \\{u, v\\}$, then for $u$, neighbors in $S_0$ is just $v$? No, $u$ and $v$ are not neighbors. So $N(u) \\cap S_0 = \\emptyset$. All 3 neighbors in $S_1$. So $u$ is invalid. Similarly $v$. So non-adjacent pairs are invalid.\nSo for $k=2$, only adjacent pairs work. Count = 12.\n$k=3$: $S_0$ has 3 vertices.\nCondition 1: Every vertex in $S_0$ has degree $\\ge 1$ in $S_0$. \nCondition 2: Every vertex in $S_1$ has degree $\\ge 1$ in $S_1$. \nSubgraphs of size 3 in cube:\n- Line of 3 (path $u-v-w$). $S_0$ induces edges $(u,v), (v,w)$. Degrees in $S_0$: $1, 2, 1$. OK. \n  Now check $S_1$ (5 vertices). We need to ensure no vertex in $S_1$ is surrounded by $S_0$. $S_0$ size 3. A vertex $z \\in S_1$ has 3 neighbors. Can $N(z) \\subseteq S_0$? Only if $S_0$ is a star of size 3 or something? Max clique is 1, max independent set is 4. Neighbors of any vertex form a $K_{1,3}$ (star). In cube, any 3 vertices can be neighbors of some $z$? Yes, the neighbors of any vertex $z$ are independent. So $S_0$ must be an independent set to be $N(z)$. But we assumed $S_0$ is a path (edges exist). So $S_0$ is not independent. Thus $N(z)$ cannot be subset of $S_0$ if $S_0$ contains an edge? Wait. The neighbors of $z$ are $a, b, c$. They are pairwise non-adjacent. If $S_0$ contains an edge, say $a, b$, then $a, b$ cannot both be in $N(z)$ because $a, b$ are not neighbors? No, $a, b$ are not neighbors is true. But being non-neighbors doesn't prevent them from being in $S_0$. The question is: Can a set of 3 vertices $S_0$ be exactly the neighbor set of some $z$? Yes, if $S_0$ is independent. If $S_0$ is a path $u-v-w$, it contains edge $(u,v)$. Can $\\{u,v,w\\}$ be the neighbors of some $z$? No, because neighbors of $z$ form an independent set. So if $S_0$ induces an edge, no vertex in $S_1$ is surrounded by $S_0$. \n  So any configuration where $S_0$ induces at least one edge is safe for $S_1$. \n  We need to count subsets of size 3 that induce no isolated vertices (min degree $\\ge 1$).\n  Total subsets of size 3: $\\binom{8}{3} = 56$. \n  Subsets with no edges (independent sets): The max independent set size is 4. \n  Number of independent sets of size 3? \n  The cube has 8 vertices. Independent sets are subsets where no two share an edge. \n  Types of independent sets of size 3:\n  - Subset of a "		             																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																								 

