Let the points be listed as $P_1=A, P_2=B, P_3=C, P_4=D, P_5=E, P_6=F$.
Any 3 non-collinear points determine a unique circle.
We need to check all subsets of 3 points from the 6. There are $\binom{6}{3} = 20$ such subsets.
We must exclude any subset where the 3 points are collinear.
The configuration is a triangle $ABC$ with midpoints $D$ (on $BC$), $E$ (on $AC$), $F$ (on $AB$).
Collinear sets of 3 points in this configuration:
