    S1 = sum of side lengths of pentagon ABCDE = 64
    S2 = sum of diagonal lengths (AC + CE + EB + BD + DA) = 72
    
    The perimeter of the midpoint pentagon is the sum of lengths of segments
    connecting midpoints of adjacent sides. By the midpoint theorem (similar to
    midline theorem in a triangle), the length of the segment connecting the
    midpoints of two sides of a triangle is half the length of the third side.
    
    Specifically:
    Length(M_AB, M_BC) = 0.5 * Length(AC)
    Length(M_BC, M_CD) = 0.5 * Length(BD)
    Length(M_CD, M_DE) = 0.5 * Length(CE)
    Length(M_DE, M_EA) = 0.5 * Length(DA)
    Length(M_EA, M_AB) = 0.5 * Length(EB)
    
    Summing these, the perimeter of the midpoint pentagon is 0.5 * (AC + BD + CE + DA + EB).
    The term in parentheses is exactly S2.
    """
    s2 = 72
    perimeter_midpoint = s2 / 2
    return str(perimeter_midpoint)

