Baby $i$ is unpoked if:
1. Baby $(i+1) \pmod n$ does NOT poke left (so they poke right).
2. Baby $(i-1) \pmod n$ does NOT poke right (so they poke left).

Let $Y_i$ be the choice of baby $i$: $Y_i \in \{L, R\}$. Probability $1/2$ for each.
$Y_{i+1} = L \implies$ Baby $i+1$ pokes $i$.

