We are given 7 arbitrary points in the plane. We want to find the maximum number of circles that can be drawn, where a circle is defined by every 4 points, provided these 4 points are concyclic (lie on the same circle).

A circle is uniquely determined by any 3 non-collinear points. Therefore, for any set of 4 points, if they are concyclic, they define exactly one circle. However, multiple sets of 4 points might lie on the same circle.

