An "ideal company" is a subset $S \subseteq F \cup M$ satisfying:
1. All girls in $S$ are liked by all boys in $S$. That is, if $g \in S \cap F$ and $b \in S \cap M$, then $g$ likes $b$.
2. $S$ is maximal with respect to this property. This means adding any element $x \notin S$ to $S$ violates condition 1.

