--- Tool Creator Reasoning ---
The number of trailing zeroes in $n!$ is determined by the exponent of the prime 5 in the prime factorization of $n!$, since there are always more factors of 2 than 5. Using Legendre's Formula, the exponent of 5 in $n!$ is given by:
