--- Tool Creator Reasoning ---
We are given $k = 3 - \frac{m}{n}$ where $m, n \in \mathbb{Z}^+$, $m \le 2000$. We want the **smallest positive value** of $k$.

$k > 0 \implies 3 - \frac{m}{n} > 0 \implies \frac{m}{n} < 3 \implies m < 3n$.
