    This implies 3n <= 2000 + r and 3n >= r + 1.
    To minimize k = r/n, we fix r and maximize n.
    Max n = floor((2000 + r) / 3).
    We iterate r starting from 1 to find the minimum k = r / n_max.
    Based on analysis, k(r) is increasing with r, so the minimum is at r=1.
    """
