{"code": "import math\nimport random\n\n# Set seed for reproducibility\nrandom.seed(42)\n\n# Define the 30-30-120 triangle\n# Vertices: A=(0,0), B=(1,0), C=(-0.5, sqrt(3)/2)\n# This triangle has side lengths 1, 1, sqrt(3).\n# Angles: Angle at A (V1) = 30, Angle at B (V2) = 120, Angle at C (V3) = 30. Wait.\n# My previous coordinate check: A(0,0), B(1,0), C(-0.5, 0.866).\n# AB = 1.\n# AC = sqrt(0.25 + 0.75) = 1.\n# BC = sqrt(2.25 + 0.75) = sqrt(3).\n# Angle at A (between AB and AC): Vector AB=(1,0), AC=(-0.5, 0.866). Dot = -0.5. Cos = -0.5. Angle = 120.\n# Angle at B: Vector BA=(-1,0), BC=(-1.5, 0.866). Dot = 1.5. Len(BA)=1, Len(BC)=sqrt(3). Cos = 1.5/sqrt(3) = sqrt(3)/2. Angle = 30.\n# Angle at C: 180 - 120 - 30 = 30.\n# So Vertex A is the 120 degree corner.\n# Let's relabel for clarity: Vertex 120 is P1=(0,0). Vertex 30 is P2=(1,0). Vertex 30 is P3=(-0.5, 0.866).\n# The container triangle is defined by P1, P2, P3.\n\nP1 = (0.0, 0.0)\nP2 = (1.0, 0.0)\nP3 = (-0.5, math.sqrt(3)/2)\n\n# Function to check if point P is inside triangle (P1, P2, P3)\ndef is_inside(P):\n    def sign1(x, y): return x**(1/2) + y**(1/2)\n    def cross(ax, ay, bx, by):\n        return ax * by - ay * bx\n    \n    # Vectors\n    vP1P2 = (P2[0]-P1[0], P2[1]-P1[1])\n    vP1P3 = (P3[0]-P1[0], P3[1]-P1[1])\n    vP1P = (P[0]-P1[0], P[1]-P1[1])\n    \n    cp1 = cross(vP1P[0], vP1P[1], vP1P2[0], vP1P2[1]) # P x AB relative to P1\n    # Check orientation. P1->P2 vs P1->P3. Cross product of AB and AC.\n    cp2 = cross(vP1P2[0], vP1P2[1], vP1P3[0], vP1P3[1]) # AB x AC\n    \n    # P must be on the same side of P1->P2 as P3\n    cp1_p2 = cross(vP1P[0], vP1P[1], vP2[0]-P2[0], vP2[1]-P2[1]) # Cross relative to P2? No.\n    \n    # Simpler: Barycentric coordinates\n    def area2(ax, ay, bx, by, cx, cy):\n        return (bx-ax)*(cy-ay) - (cx-ax)*(by-ay)\n    \n    area123 = abs(area2(P1[0], P1[1], P2[0], P2[1], P3[0], P3[1]))\n    area12P = abs(area2(P1[0], P1[1], P2[0], P2[1], P[0], P[1]))\n    area13P = abs(area2(P1[0], P1[1], P3[0], P3[1], P[0], P[1]))\n    area23P = abs(area2(P2[0], P2[1], P3[0], P3[1], P[0], P[1]))\n    \n    eps = 1e-9\n    return abs(area12P + area13P + area23P - area123) < eps\n\ndef get_third_point(p1, p2, angle_deg):\n    rad = math.radians(angle_deg)\n    dx, dy = p2[0]-p1[0], p2[1]-p1[1]\n    return (p1[0] + dx*math.cos(rad) - dy*math.sin(rad),\n            p1[1] + dx*math.sin(rad) + dy*math.cos(rad))\n\ndef rand_pt_in_triangle():\n    r1 = random.random()\n    r2 = random.random()\n    if r1 + r2 > 1:\n        r1, r2 = 1-r1, 1-r2\n    # P = r1*P2 + r2*P3 + (1-r1-r2)*P1\n    x = r1*P2[0] + r2*P3[0] + (1-r1-r2)*P1[0]\n    y = r1*P2[1] + r2*P3[1] + (1-r1-r2)*P1[1]\n    return (x, y)\n\nbest_side = 0.0\nbest_area = 0.0\n\n# Monte Carlo Search\nfor _ in range(500000):\n    p1 = rand_pt_in_triangle()\n    p2 = rand_pt_in_triangle()\n    d2 = (p1[0]-p2[0])**2 + **(p1[1]-p2[1])2\n    d = math.sqrt(d2)\n    if d < 1e-6: continue\n    \n    # Check two possible equilateral triangles\n    for ang in [60, -60]:\n        p3 = get_third_point(p1, p2, ang)\n        if is_inside(p3):\n            if d > best_side:\n                best_side = d\n                best_area = (d**2 * math.sqrt(3)) / 4\n\n# Container triangle area (30-30-120)\ncontainer_area = 0.5 * 1 * 1 * math.sin(math.radians(120))\n\nprint(f'Max side in corner: {best_side}')\nprint(f'Max area in corner: {best_area}')\nprint(f'Container area: {container_area}')\nprint(f'Ratio: {best_area/container_area}')\n\n# Hexagon context: Hexagon Area = 1.\n# 30-30-120 corner area is exactly 1/6 of the hexagon.\n# T1 takes 0.5. Remaining 0.5 is distributed in 3 corners (1/6 each).\n# T2, T3, T4 are the largest in these corners.\n\narea_T1 = 0.5\ncorner_area_hex = 1/6\nactual_T2_area = (best_area / container_area) * corner_area_hex\n\ncoverage_4 = area_T1 + 3 * actual_T2_area\n\nprint(f'Hexagon Area: 1')\nprint(f'T1 Area: {area_T1}')\nprint(f'T2 Area: {actual_T2_area}')\nprint(f'Coverage after 4 triangles: {coverage_4}')\nprint(f'Is >= 0.9? {coverage_4 >= 0.9}')\n"}

