Since the set of digits is the same, the condition $0 \le d_i \le 3$ is always satisfied for base $b$ as long as $|b| - 1 \ge 3$, i.e., $|b| \ge 4$. If $|b| < 4$, the digit constraints might be violated unless all digits beyond the valid range are 0. However, since the representations are identical digit-for-digit from $0$ to $k$, we must check consistency.
